  "description": "Add-on for IntentSharp: move changeable rules into YAML or JSON intent files (LLM prompt instructions, result shape, rules, examples). A saved edit applies to the next call: no rebuild, restart or redeploy. Intent files are versioned documents: an earlier version can be made the running one again (revert), and every run is tagged with the intent's name, version and source file. Your code names the intent and reads the answer as text, a yes or no, a number, a date, a list, a .NET type registered in code, or JSON that must match a JSON schema. Every reply is checked in your process against the file's rules, and structured output with a JSON schema shape against its whole schema; a failed check goes back to the model on the next attempt. The folder is watched: calls already running finish on the old version, and a file that fails to load keeps the last good definition in force while the application runs. A new .NET result type, a result shape the calling code's type cannot read, a new named code check, or code that calls a new intent by name still needs a release. Reload is tested on local folders. Add this package to IntentSharp when intents live in files, or when named intents are defined in code in a catalog (InMemoryIntentCatalog). A project whose calls are inline or [AIIntent] methods needs only IntentSharp, without this package's YAML and JSON Schema dependencies. IntentSharp.Extensions.AI brings this package with it. Our estimate for IntentSharp in a typical business application is 20 to 40% less application code. Commercial software, not open source: evaluate free for 30 days on development and test systems; after that, business use needs a paid license, and production use needs one from the first day (intentsharp.com/pricing).",
  "iconFile": "icon.png",
